cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its predictions, please cite it as below."
title: "protein-stack: function prediction beyond the twilight zone with gated AlphaFold structure fusion"
authors:
  - family-names: Thotlapalli
    given-names: Ahmed
    affiliation: "King's College London"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8119-3312"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-25"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - protein function prediction
  - AlphaFold
  - Foldseek
  - knowledge graph
  - Gene Ontology
  - dark proteome
abstract: >
  A reproducible pipeline that fuses sequence homology, AlphaFold structural
  similarity, InterPro domains, and STRING interactions to predict protein
  function under a strict evidence-provenance discipline. Structural transfer
  measurably improves prediction below 30% sequence identity; an
  identity-gated fusion beats every single evidence stream; and a time-split
  validation against archived GOA releases shows 40.7% top-1
  molecular-function precision (permutation p = 0.001) with monotone
  confidence calibration, including genuine falsifications via experimental
  NOT-qualifier annotations.
